      "message": "Looking through the code again, I think this should actually be in the `rollback_add_entropy` function (which is called below). The reason is that we do have other places that call `rollback_add_entropy`, such as `command_rollback_add_entropy`.\n\nAlso, we have a unit test in `test/rollback_entropy.c` that verifies the entropy written to the rollback section. We should add a check to make sure OTP was provisioned. That\u0027s not going to tell us much if we\u0027ve already set the OTP bits, so we could [mock the `otp_key_provision` function](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/HEAD/common/mock/README.md) in the test and make sure it is called.",
